{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Hardware Peripheral Devices"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about hardware peripheral devices."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the user interface, supported on the prototype assessment, determining the inputs and outputs required in the design and defining the navigation guidelines, according to the user's needs. Identifies different hardware components and peripheral devices."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about peripheral devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 6 devices and classify them into internal and external peripheral devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a description of each device you have chosen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show those descriptions to your instructor and classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about peripheral devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I classify peripheral devices in two categories: internal and external."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe each peripheral device that I chose. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "peripheral"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that can be included in the computer for extra features "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let me describe the types of peripheral devices."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "input"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "devices that can register information in a computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some peripheral devices are used for input which allow the computer to register information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "output"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "devices that can show the information from a computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Other computer peripherals are used for output which allow you to get information from the computer. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "add-on "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extra features that can be added in a device"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is not mandatory for you to have an add-on since the computer should work normally without one."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "performance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way in which something works"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can add some peripheral devices that allow to expand your computer's performance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attach"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to add something extra to a device"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are devices that are attached to your computer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use <strong>subject relative clauses</strong> to provide more information about the subject of the sentence.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Whenever we want to provide extra information about a subject, we use the relative pronouns <strong>who, which, that. </strong>In a <strong>subject relative clause, </strong>you always put the verb after the relative pronoun.</p> <p>Let&rsquo;s see the grammatical structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>relative pronoun</strong> + verb + complement</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>Those are devices <strong>which</strong> improve the performance of the computer.</i></p> <p>Let&rsquo;s compare these two sentences:</p> <p><i>We use a hardware. The hardware expands the computer&rsquo;s abilities.</i></p> <p><i>We use a hardware<strong> that</strong> expands the computer&rsquo;s abilities.</i></p> <p>As you can see, we can include more information in just one sentence using subject relative clauses.</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p><strong>Relative pronoun</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p><strong>To talk about:</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"People\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Things\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"People/Things\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can add some peripheral devices that allow to expand your computer's performance."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are devices that are attached to your computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some peripheral devices are used for input which allow the computer to register information."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may need an external hard drive which works for both input and output."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Computer Peripherals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Computer peripherals </strong>are supplementary devices that you can add to your computer to improve it.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>As we all know, the concept <strong>hardware </strong>refers to all physical parts of a certain device. A <strong>Computer peripheral </strong>is a hardware that is attached to the computer in order to obtain extra features.</p> <p>It&rsquo;s important to take into account that these peripherals are not necessary for the regular functioning of a computer. They are optional devices which allow the users to obtain extra benefits.</p> <p>There are two types of peripheral devices, Internal peripheral devices operate inside the computer&rsquo;s case, and external peripheral devices operate outside the case. They both provide input and output services.</p> <p>Finally, any peripheral device has to come with a driver that allows the computer to detect the device and let it work properly.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Examples of Peripheral Devices&nbsp; </strong></p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Input</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Output</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Both</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mouse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Monitor\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"External hard drive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Keyboard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Printer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are devices that are attached to your computer. We have input devices and output devices which give you extra benefits."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is not mandatory for you to have an add-on since the computer should work normally without one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The main difference between them is the way they are connected to your computer."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Nicolas:</strong> Welcome to <em>Computerworld, </em>how can I help you?</p>\n<p><strong>Stella: </strong>I&rsquo;m looking forward to upgrading my computer. It is used for everything at home and I need to check how I can improve it.</p>\n<p><strong>Nicolas: </strong>Ok, we can add some peripheral devices that allow you to expand your computer&rsquo;s performance.</p>\n<p><strong>Stella: </strong>Sounds great! But, what are peripheral devices exactly?</p>"}, {"time": "24000", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Nicolas: </strong>They are devices that are attached to your computer. We have input devices and output devices which give you extra benefits. However, it is not mandatory for you to have an add-on since the computer should work normally without one. Now, there are internal and external peripherals, which ones do you prefer?</p>\n<p><strong>Stella: </strong>I don&rsquo;t know, what is the difference between them?</p>\n<p><strong>Nicolas: </strong>The main difference between them is the way they are connected to your computer. An internal peripheral goes inside the CPU&rsquo;s case such as sound or video cards, and an external peripheral can be connected using the different slots that computers have for this purpose, such as flash drives or cameras.</p>\n<p><strong>Stella: </strong>Well, what do you think I should get then?</p>"}, {"time": "73000", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Nicolas: </strong>It depends on what you want your computer to do. Let me describe the types of peripheral devices.</p>\n<p><strong>Stella:</strong> That would help a lot.</p>\n<p><strong>Nicolas:</strong> Some peripheral devices are used for input which allows the computer to register information. The most common devices are computer mice and keyboards. However, there are some others like microphones, scanners or fingerprint readers. Other computer peripherals are used for output, which allows you to get information from the computer such as the monitor. You could get a printer or some speakers. Also, you may need an external hard drive which works for both input and output. So, what exactly do you need?</p>\n<p><strong>Stella: </strong>I want an external hard drive!</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le01ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about peripheral devices."}, {"type": "L